From: Cosmopod OS Build Team <builds@cosmopod.invalid>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 23:55:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] libfdt: keep memchr results const

The overlay fixup strings come from a const property buffer.  Newer glibc
headers preserve that qualifier through memchr, so make the separator pointer
const as well.  No data is modified through it.

Upstream-Status: Pending

---
 libfdt/fdt_overlay.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libfdt/fdt_overlay.c b/libfdt/fdt_overlay.c
index 5c0c398..927d47d 100644
--- a/libfdt/fdt_overlay.c
+++ b/libfdt/fdt_overlay.c
@@ -430,7 +430,8 @@ static int overlay_fixup_phandle(void *fdt, void *fdto, int symbols_off,
 		const char *fixup_str = value;
 		uint32_t path_len, name_len;
 		uint32_t fixup_len;
-		char *sep, *endptr;
+		const char *sep;
+		char *endptr;
 		int poffset, ret;
 
 		fixup_end = memchr(value, '\0', len);
-- 
2.43.0
